  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Which of the following is equivalent to\n\n\\[\\sqrt{\\dfrac{x}{1-\\dfrac{x-1}{x}}}\\]\n\nwhen \\(x \\lt 0?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-x\\)",
    "B": "\\(x\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{x}{2}}\\)",
    "E": "\\(x\\sqrt{-1}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "First simplify the denominator inside the radical. Since \\(x<0\\), we have \\(x\\ne0\\), so\n\\[\n1-\\frac{x-1}{x}\n=\\frac{x-(x-1)}{x}\n=\\frac1x.\n\\]\nThis denominator is also nonzero. Hence the radicand becomes\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{1/x}=x^2>0.\n\\]\nThe square-root symbol denotes the nonnegative square root, so\n\\[\n\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|=-x\n\\]\nbecause \\(x<0\\). Therefore the expression is \\(\\boxed{-x}\\), choice A.",
